Description: GHSA-7qpv-r5mr-78m4 (CVE-2026-17543): SQL injection through pg_convert(), pg_insert(), pg_update(), pg_delete() and pg_select(): values escaped with PQescapeStringConn() were quoted as E'...', where a backslash escapes the quote, while PQescapeStringConn() doubles backslashes only with standard_conforming_strings off; they are quoted as '...' now.
Origin: php-src commit 6a80d9d36a5e of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports) (27.07.2026, Ilija Tovilo, cherry-pick of ab048bd83b57), with the expected results of the pgsql tests

diff --git a/ext/pgsql/pgsql.c b/ext/pgsql/pgsql.c
index d37bde7d..54c4a634 100644
--- a/ext/pgsql/pgsql.c
+++ b/ext/pgsql/pgsql.c
@@ -5750,7 +5750,6 @@ static int php_pgsql_add_quotes(zval *src, zend_bool should_free TSRMLS_DC)
 	assert(Z_TYPE_P(src) == IS_STRING);
 	assert(should_free == 1 || should_free == 0);
 
-	smart_str_appendc(&str, 'E');
 	smart_str_appendc(&str, '\'');
 	smart_str_appendl(&str, Z_STRVAL_P(src), Z_STRLEN_P(src));
 	smart_str_appendc(&str, '\'');
@@ -6040,7 +6039,6 @@ PHP_PGSQL_API int php_pgsql_convert(PGconn *pg_link, const char *table_name, con
 							/* PostgreSQL ignores \0 */
 							Z_TYPE_P(new_val) = IS_STRING;
 							tmp = (char *)safe_emalloc(Z_STRLEN_PP(val), 2, 1);
-							/* better to use PGSQLescapeLiteral since PGescapeStringConn does not handle special \ */
 							Z_STRLEN_P(new_val) = (int)PQescapeStringConn(pg_link, tmp, Z_STRVAL_PP(val), Z_STRLEN_PP(val), NULL);
 							Z_STRVAL_P(new_val) = tmp;
 							php_pgsql_add_quotes(new_val, 1 TSRMLS_CC);
